        plugins register elements, templates and fonts into the registry
        the renderer is an interface — PDF today, HTML or a viewer later
        this diagram is the diagram: Rect + Ellipse + Arrow + Text

// --------------------------------------------------------------- 8 · style

SlidezTwoColumns:
    Title: "Style cascade"

    Bullets:
        Column: 0
        Slides: sets deck-wide defaults
        a slide overrides for its children
        an element overrides for itself
        nothing set anywhere -> class defaults
        fonts resolve by name from the registry
            Manrope, Montserrat, Liberation, Mono — or yours

    Code: "Slides:\n    Font: Manrope\n    Size: 24\n\nMySlide:\n    Color: \"#E8ECEF\"   # slide-level\n\n    Text: inherits everything\n    Text: except what it sets\n        Size: 40\n"
        Column: 1
        Size: 14.5
        Fill: "#131A21"

// ----------------------------------------------------------- 9 · templates

SlidezTwoColumns:
    Title: "Templates are Slide subclasses"

    Bullets:
        Column: 0
        Size: 20
        a template is just Python inheritance
            TitleSlide, BulletSlide, ImageSideSlide...
            use it by class name: "TitleSlide:"
        chrome — footers, page numbers — is a mixin
        this deck's opener is the code on the right
            three roles: title, subtitle, company

    Code: "@register\nclass SlidezTitleSlide(TitleSlide):\n    background = \"media/bg_title.jpg\"\n\n    roles = TitleSlide.roles + (\n        \"company\",)\n    title_scale = 4.2\n    company_pos = (0.30, 0.78)\n"
        Column: 1
        Size: 13.5
        Fill: "#131A21"

// ------------------------------------------------------------- 10 · plugins

SlidezSlide:
    Title: "Plugins: elements from scratch"

    Code: "@register\nclass Stat(Element):\n    number = \"\"\n    caption = \"\"\n\n    def render_flow(self, ctx):\n        big = ctx.get_font(\"Manrope\").with_size(46)\n        ctx.text_block([[ (self.number, True) ]],\n                       x, ctx.y, w, big, ACCENT, \"center\")\n"
        Size: 15
        Fill: "#131A21"
        Width: 0.62

    Bullets:
        Position: [0.68, 0.30]
        Width: 0.26
        Size: 19
        a plugin is one module imported by main.py
        class attributes become language properties
        render through ctx: fonts, wrapping, shapes
        the numbers on the next slide are this exact element

// -------------------------------------------------------------- 11 · stats

SlidezImageRight:
    Title: "The core, by the numbers"

    Stat: "960"
        Caption: "lines of core code"

    Stat: "1"
        Caption: "pip dependency (fpdf2)"

    Stat: "9"
        Caption: "core elements — plus your own"

    Image: "media/chart.png"
        Role: image
        Size: [0.52]

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- 12 · meta

SlidezSlide:
    Title: "This deck, in Slidez"

    Bullets:
        MarkerColor: "#61AFEF"
        the opener and closer are one template, three roles
        the comparison slide is two columns, one flag per element
        every code sample is the Code element — real indentation, no escapes
        the architecture diagram is five rects and five arrows
        backgrounds, footer and page numbers come from a chrome mixin
        the big numbers are a custom element, defined in ten lines
        total: one .sldz file, one theme.py, four small images

// ----------------------------------------------------------- 13 · quickstart

SlidezSlide:
    Title: "Getting started"

    Code: "git clone https://github.com/e-ivkov/slidez.git\ncd slidez\npython3 -m venv .venv\n.venv/bin/pip install -r requirements.txt\n.venv/bin/python main.py presentations/slidez_deck/deck.sldz\n\"\n# then open plugins/basic.py and make it yours —\n# it is written to be forked, not configured\n"
        Size: 15
        Fill: "#131A21"
        Width: 0.80

    Bullets:
        Position: [0.06, 0.80]
        Width: 0.88
        Size: 19
        write deck.sldz, render, commit, diff, repeat
        when the core lacks a feature — that is your feature to add

// --------------------------------------------------------------- 14 · close

SlidezTitleSlide:
    Image: "media/logo.png"
        Position: [0.07, 0.38]
        Size: [0.15, 0.15]

    Text: "Text in. PDF out."
        Role: title
        Font: Manrope
        Bold: true
        Size: 64

    Text: "clone it, skim it, extend it"
        Role: subtitle

    Text: "github.com/e-ivkov/slidez — a compiler sized for humans and AIs"
        Role: company
        Color: "#9AA7B0"
